sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title YuPay — Telegram broadcast send (scheduler-driven fan-out)

    participant A as Admin SPA
    participant API as FastAPI /admin/broadcasts
    participant SVC as broadcasts.service
    participant DB as Postgres
    participant SCH as Scheduler (broadcast_dispatch, every ~5s)
    participant TG as Telegram Bot API

    Note over A,DB: Compose + send now (schedule is the same, plus a promote step)

    A->>API: POST /admin/broadcasts {title, body_html, media...} (Idempotency-Key)
    API->>SVC: create_draft(...)
    SVC->>DB: INSERT broadcasts (status='draft')
    A->>API: POST /admin/broadcasts/{id}/test (Idempotency-Key)
    API->>TG: sendMessage/sendPhoto to admin's own chat
    TG-->>API: 200
    A->>API: POST /admin/broadcasts/{id}/send (Idempotency-Key)
    API->>SVC: mark_send_now(id)
    SVC->>SVC: sanitize.validate_body(body_html) — re-validate stored body
    SVC->>DB: UPDATE broadcasts SET status='sending'
    API-->>A: 200 {status: sending}
    Note over API,SCH: status flip only — no queue, no message sent yet

    loop every ~5s tick
        SCH->>DB: UPDATE scheduled → sending WHERE scheduled_at <= now()
        SCH->>DB: SELECT id FROM broadcasts WHERE status='sending' ORDER BY started_at LIMIT 5

        alt first tick for this broadcast
            SCH->>DB: INSERT broadcast_recipients (snapshot)<br/>FROM telegram_links JOIN users<br/>WHERE bot_blocked_at IS NULL [AND locale=:f]<br/>ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
            SCH->>DB: UPDATE broadcasts SET total_recipients=count, started_at=now()
        end

        SCH->>DB: SELECT id FROM broadcast_recipients<br/>WHERE status='pending' LIMIT 250 (chunk)

        loop each recipient in chunk, paced ~25/s
            SCH->>DB: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED (claim one row)
            SCH->>TG: sendMessage/sendPhoto/sendVideo/sendAnimation/sendDocument
            alt 200 OK
                TG-->>SCH: 200 {file_id?}
                SCH->>DB: UPDATE recipient SET status='sent', sent_at=now()<br/>(+ UPDATE broadcasts.media_file_id on first media send)
                SCH->>DB: UPDATE broadcasts SET sent_count = sent_count + 1
            else 403 blocked/deactivated
                TG-->>SCH: 403
                SCH->>DB: UPDATE recipient SET status='blocked'
                SCH->>DB: UPDATE telegram_links SET bot_blocked_at=now()
                SCH->>DB: UPDATE broadcasts SET blocked_count = blocked_count + 1
            else 429 rate limited
                TG-->>SCH: 429 {retry_after}
                SCH->>SCH: sleep(retry_after), retry same recipient once
            else 400 bad request, sent_count == 0
                TG-->>SCH: 400
                SCH->>DB: UPDATE recipient SET status='failed', error=...
                SCH->>DB: UPDATE broadcasts SET status='failed', last_error=..., finished_at=now()
                Note over SCH: abort whole broadcast — stop claiming further recipients
            else 5xx / network, or 400 after a prior success
                TG-->>SCH: 5xx / error
                SCH->>SCH: retry up to 2x, then give up
                SCH->>DB: UPDATE recipient SET status='failed', error=...
                SCH->>DB: UPDATE broadcasts SET failed_count = failed_count + 1
            end
            Note over SCH,DB: row transition commits before the next send<br/>(crash window <= 1 recipient, at-least-once)
        end

        alt no pending rows remain
            SCH->>DB: UPDATE broadcasts SET status='sent', finished_at=now()
        end
    end

    loop while status in (sending, scheduled)
        A->>API: GET /admin/broadcasts/{id} (poll)
        API-->>A: {status, sent_count, failed_count, blocked_count, total_recipients}
    end
